-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/901930d4-6a42-578f-845f-ee71134ac9fe
-- title:
--   Type splitting of the truncated twisted kernel, with domain independence
-- statement:
--   Setting. Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields which is Galois, let $\alpha,\beta$ be real numbers, and write $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_L)$ for `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 L) L`, the general linear group of degree $2$ over the adele ring of $L$. For $g$ in this group let $\|\det g\|$ denote [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm L`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19) of $\det g$, i.e. the value at the idele $\det g$ of the Haar character of $\mathbf{A}_L$; the determinant slab is the set of $g$ with $\|\det g\|\in[\alpha,\beta]$. Two subsets $\Phi_L$ and $\Phi_0$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_L)$ are given, together with two groups of hypotheses: the slab conditions `hΦs` and `hΦ₀s`, stating that $\Phi_L$ and $\Phi_0$ are contained in the determinant slab, and the fundamental-domain conditions `hΦ` and `hΦ₀`, stating that each of $\Phi_L$ and $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the action of the range of `globalPoints (𝓞 L) L` (the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ under the diagonal embedding induced by $L\to\mathbf{A}_L$) with respect to the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` restricted to the determinant slab.
--
--   Further data: a measure $\nu_{Z_L}$ on the idele group $\mathbf{A}_L^\times$ (for a given measurable structure on it) and an arbitrary subset $\Omega_L\subseteq\mathbf{A}_L^\times$, on neither of which any condition is imposed; a homomorphism $\xi_L$ from the full idele group of $L$, presented as the top subgroup of $\mathbf{A}_L^\times$, to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, with no continuity requirement; a datum $D$ of type [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent (𝓞 L) K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28), that is, a homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)\to\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathrm{ring}}(\mathbf{A}_L)$ whose value at each $\tau$ is continuous and agrees with $\tau$ on the image of $L$; an element $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ together with the hypothesis `hgen` that every $\tau\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$); a finite set $S$ of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$; a function $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$; and a family $\varphi_S$ assigning to each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$ a complex function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$.
--
--   Write $\sigma_{\mathbf{A}}=$ [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14) for the endomorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_L)$ obtained by applying $D.\mathrm{act}\,\sigma$ entrywise, $c(z)=$ [`AutomorphicForm.centralScalar (𝓞 L) L z`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L18) for the central scalar matrix attached to an idele $z$, and, for a function $\phi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_L)$,
--   $$K_\sigma(x,y)=\textstyle\sum^{\mathrm{f}}_{\gamma\in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)}\phi\bigl(x^{-1}\cdot\gamma\cdot\sigma_{\mathbf{A}}(y)\bigr)$$
--   for [`AutomorphicForm.twistedAdelicKernel`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedAdelicKernel.html#L13), the unconditional sum over $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ (embedded by `globalPoints`). Let $u(t)=$ [`AutomorphicForm.unipotentGL2 t`](def/AutomorphicForm_ConstantTerm.html#L17) be the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}1&t\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, let $H=$ [`NumberField.AdelicHeight.adelicHeight L`](def/NumberField_AdelicHeight.html#L158) be the product of the archimedean and finite adelic heights, and let $\nu$ be the measure component of `productionPinsOf L ΦL (fun M => levelOne (𝓞 L) L M ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L) (fun w => heckeGen (𝓞 L) L w) (adelicBox L)`, namely the additive adelic Haar measure of $L$ conditioned on `adelicBox L` (the adeles whose archimedean part lies in the fundamental parallelotope of the Minkowski lattice basis and whose finite part is integral at every prime), taken with respect to the Borel structure on $\mathbf{A}_L$. For a function $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_L)$ the constant term is $C f(g)=\int f(u(t)g)\,d\nu(t)$, the high set at level $T$ is $\{g: T<H(g)\}$, and the truncation is $\Lambda^T f(g)=f(g)-\mathbf{1}_{\{H>T\}}(g)\,Cf(g)$ ([`AutomorphicForm.lambdaT`](def/AutomorphicForm_TruncationOperator.html#L48)).
--
--   Assertion. For every finite set $T$ of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$, every assignment $v\mapsto w_v$ of a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying over $v$, every function $v\mapsto n_v$ into $\mathbb{N}$, every family $r_{T}$ assigning to each $v$ a tuple $(r_{v,0},\dots,r_{v,n_v-1})$ of elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$, every family $v\mapsto z_v\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$, all functions $v\mapsto k_v$, $v\mapsto j_v$ into $\mathbb{N}$, and all functions $\phi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_L)$ and $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles of $L$, the following holds. Assume `IsSemiLocalFactorization K L (S ∪ T)` for $\phi$, $\varphi_a$, $\varphi_f$ and the family of semi-local factors which at $v\in T$ is
--   $$x\longmapsto \sum_{\iota:\{0,\dots,k_v-1\}\to\{0,\dots,n_v-1\}}\mathbf{1}_{\Omega_v}\bigl(g_{v,\iota}^{-1}x\bigr),\qquad g_{v,\iota}=\text{image in }\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)\text{ of } r_{v,\iota(0)}\cdots r_{v,\iota(k_v-1)}\,z_v^{\,j_v},$$
--   the image being taken by first embedding $\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ into $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles of $L$ by [`AdelicDock.localEmbed`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L97) (splice at $w_v$, identity elsewhere) and then applying `semiLocalComponent K L v`, and $\Omega_v=$ `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` being the set of elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ such that both the element and its inverse have all entries in the image of `HeightOneSpectrum.tensorAdicCompletionIntegersTo K L (𝓞 L) v`; and which at $v\notin T$ is $\varphi_S\,v$. Thus it is assumed that $\varphi_a$ is an archimedean test factor (given by a smooth function of the archimedean matrix entries, of compact support), that $\varphi_f$ is locally constant with compact support, that each of these factors at the primes of $S\cup T$ is locally constant with compact support, that $\varphi_f(h)$ equals the product over $v\in S\cup T$ of the factors evaluated at the semi-local components of $h$ whenever all semi-local components of $h$ outside $S\cup T$ are integral, that $\varphi_f(h)=0$ as soon as some semi-local component outside $S\cup T$ fails to be integral, and that $\phi(g)=\varphi_a(g_\infty)\varphi_f(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$ for all $g$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists $R_0\in\mathbb{R}$ such that for every real $R\ge R_0$ both of the following hold.
--
--   First, for all $x\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_L)$ and all ideles $z$, with $T=e^{R}$ as truncation parameter,
--   $$\Lambda^{e^R}\bigl(y\mapsto K_\sigma(x,y)\bigr)\bigl(c(z)x\bigr)=A+\bigl(B-\mathbf{1}_{\{H>e^R\}}\,C\beta_1\bigr)\bigl(c(z)x\bigr)+\bigl(D'-\mathbf{1}_{\{H>e^R\}}\,C\beta_{\neq 1}\bigr)\bigl(c(z)x\bigr),$$
--   where: $A$, $B$, $D'$ are the unconditional sums of $\phi\bigl(x^{-1}\cdot\delta\cdot\sigma_{\mathbf{A}}(c(z)x)\bigr)$ over those $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ for which there is a $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ with [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766) of the $\sigma$-conjugacy class of $\delta$ equal to the conjugacy class of $\gamma$, and $\gamma$ lying respectively in `ellipticCell K ∪ centralCell K` (characteristic polynomial without root in $K$, or a scalar matrix), in `unipotentCell K` (non-scalar with characteristic polynomial a square $(X-a)^2$), and in `hyperbolicCell K` (characteristic polynomial $(X-a)(X-b)$ with $a\neq b$); and $\beta_1$, $\beta_{\neq 1}$ are the partial kernels
--   $$\beta(y)=\sum^{\mathrm{f}}_{\delta}\phi\bigl(x^{-1}\cdot\delta\cdot\sigma_{\mathbf{A}}(y)\bigr),$$
--   the sum being over those $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with lower-left entry $0$ and with $N_{L/K}(\delta_{00}/\delta_{11})=1$ for $\beta_1$, respectively $N_{L/K}(\delta_{00}/\delta_{11})\neq 1$ for $\beta_{\neq1}$, and $C$ denoting the constant term above, the indicator being that of the high set $\{g: e^R<H(g)\}$ and both being evaluated at $c(z)x$.
--
--   Second, the central-elliptic contribution has the same integral over the two fundamental domains:
--   $$\int_{\Phi_0}\!\!\int_{\Omega_L}\xi_L(z)\,A(x,z)\,d\nu_{Z_L}(z)\,d\mu(x)=\int_{\Phi_L}\!\!\int_{\Omega_L}\xi_L(z)\,A(x,z)\,d\nu_{Z_L}(z)\,d\mu(x),$$
--   where $\mu=$ `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L`, $\xi_L(z)$ is the complex number underlying the value of $\xi_L$ at $z$ regarded as an element of the top subgroup, and $A(x,z)$ is the sum over $\delta$ described above whose norm class meets `ellipticCell K ∪ centralCell K`, with summand $\phi\bigl(x^{-1}\cdot\delta\cdot\sigma_{\mathbf{A}}(c(z)x)\bigr)$.
--
--   This is the geometric-side bookkeeping step of the $\sigma$-twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension $L/K$: the twisted kernel, truncated at one cusp by subtracting the constant term on the high part of the adelic height, is decomposed according to the type (central or elliptic, unipotent, hyperbolic) of the conjugacy class in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ attached to the $\sigma$-conjugacy class of the summation variable by the norm class map, the two parabolic types being paired with the constant terms of the corresponding upper-triangular partial kernels. It is used downstream both for the treatment of the twisted parabolic terms, where the hyperbolic and unipotent contributions are recombined, and for the central-elliptic term, whose integral against the character $\xi_L$ the second conjunct shows to be independent of the chosen fundamental domain inside the determinant slab.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_forall_exists_lambdaT_twistedAdelicKernel_eq_finsum_add_sub_indicator_constantTerm_add.lean

